[Music]  there is no question that justice breyer  for whom i have great respect  should retire at the end of this term  i mean my goodness have we not learned  our lesson just to be clear you do think  that justice steven breyer should retire  at the end of this term i'm inclined to  say yes i do believe that he should  retire prior to the midterms i think  that would be best for our country  progressive democrats got what they  wanted supreme court justice stephen  breyer announced his resignation  ironically this comes the same week  nancy pelosi announced she would run  again she's been in the house for 35  years  which is seven years longer than justice  breyer has been on the supreme court  progressives were in a hurry to get rid  of justice breyer who was 83 but the top  three democrats in the house  are all over the age of 80 themselves  and they don't seem to be going anywhere  irony aside briar's retirement does give  president biden a chance to fulfill at  least one campaign promise as the  midterms near joining us now is senator  marshall blackburn from the great state  of tennessee who sits on the senate  judiciary  committee welcome to you senator another  supreme court confirmation hearing i i  hope  some of your colleagues on the committee  treat this nominee with more respect  than they treated  amy coney barrett what do you think  what we know is that this is going to be  one of those fights that we will have  as to how the senate goes about  providing advice and consent which is  our responsibility and our  constitutional duty and i agree with you  it would be nice if we would see this  approached as a respectful process  respectful to the institution of the  senate and respectful to the  constitution of the united states and  make certain that we do the vetting that  is necessary  that we spend the time reviewing rulings  and writings and opinions and listening  to speeches our duty is to make certain  that we have constitutionalists  that go to the bench people that are  going to be fair that are going to  uphold that constitution and the rule of  law and trade to be certain that we do  not put people  on the supreme court or the federal  bench who are going to be activist  judges and are going to make rulings the  way they would like to see things be  rather than making rulings based on the  rule of law  you know senator  even senators that serve a long long  time and we've had quite a few in south  carolina the likelihood is that a  supreme court justice will serve longer  than any senator  so as you go through the advice and  consent process what are you looking for  in a nominee and how does that process  work  in your own mind as you're vetting these  nominees  yes and as we get a nominee then what we  will do is look at that record of their  rulings and their opinions their  writings and pull that around as and ask  those questions is this based on the  constitution is it based on the rule of  law has this person served as a judge  you know trey one of the issues we've  had with the biden administration when  it comes to putting judges on the  federal bench for district courts or  appellate courts is they are sending us  people who are to the left they're  radical  they have radical writings or opinions  they're outside of the mainstream some  of them have been very active on social  media  and have been  anti-conservatives and i have not had  that even-handed temperament  that you know so well  is expected of judges to think things  through many times we have people  presented to us who have never spent one  minute  serving as a judge in any capacity at  the city the county the state level but  they're trying to put them on the  federal bench but the vetting process is  really such an integral part of  selecting a judge who as you said this  is a lifetime appointment and i really  do feel a little bit for justice breyer  because it appears that he was being  pushed out the white house for political  gain  revealed that he was looking to retire  they did not wait for him to make this  announcement they made that announcement  on their time and in their manner to go  ahead and push him out so that they  could have a better  day in the news cycle which has not been  good for them this year yeah you know  senator i i'm so old now i've got a lot  of friends who are judges and the best  ones have this one characteristic and  comment and that is humility to know  they're not legislators they're not  super legislators it takes humility to  be a judge so  i love confirmation hearings i can't  wait to watch  you and i think there may even be a guy  from south carolina on your committee i  may watch him  too but  i look forward to it thank you for your  service hey sean hannity here hey click  here to subscribe to fox news youtube  page and catch our hottest interviews  and most compelling analysis you will  not get it anywhere else

